8.2 JMX exporter (sur dbk70-72 et dbz70-71)
a) Installer l’agent (sur les 5 machines)
mkdir -p /opt/jmx_exporter /etc/jmx_exporter && cp /opt/bundle/artifacts/monitoring/jmx_prometheus_javaagent-1.6.0.jar /opt/jmx_exporter/ && chmod 755 /opt/jmx_exporter /etc/jmx_exporter && chmod 644 /opt/jmx_exporter/*.jar && restorecon -R /opt/jmx_exporter /etc/jmx_exporter
b) Règles pour les brokers (sur dbk70-72)

Ces règles transforment les métriques JMX de Kafka en noms Prometheus. Elles incluent les métriques du quorum KRaft (raft-metrics).

cat > /etc/jmx_exporter/kafka-broker.yml <<'EOF'
lowercaseOutputName: true
lowercaseOutputLabelNames: true
rules:
  # KRaft (quorum)
  - pattern: 'kafka.server<type=raft-metrics><>([a-z-]+)'
    name: kafka_server_raft_$1
    type: GAUGE
  # Cas particuliers
  - pattern: 'kafka.server<type=(.+), name=(.+), clientId=(.+), topic=(.+), partition=(.*)><>Value'
    name: kafka_server_$1_$2
    type: GAUGE
    labels: { clientId: "$3", topic: "$4", partition: "$5" }
  - pattern: 'kafka.server<type=(.+), name=(.+), clientId=(.+), brokerHost=(.+), brokerPort=(.+)><>Value'
    name: kafka_server_$1_$2
    type: GAUGE
    labels: { clientId: "$3", broker: "$4:$5" }
  - pattern: 'kafka.coordinator.(\w+)<type=(.+), name=(.+)><>Value'
    name: kafka_coordinator_$1_$2_$3
    type: GAUGE
  # Compteurs "PerSec"
  - pattern: 'kafka.(\w+)<type=(.+), name=(.+)PerSec\w*, (.+)=(.+), (.+)=(.+)><>Count'
    name: kafka_$1_$2_$3_total
    type: COUNTER
    labels: { "$4": "$5", "$6": "$7" }
  - pattern: 'kafka.(\w+)<type=(.+), name=(.+)PerSec\w*, (.+)=(.+)><>Count'
    name: kafka_$1_$2_$3_total
    type: COUNTER
    labels: { "$4": "$5" }
  - pattern: 'kafka.(\w+)<type=(.+), name=(.+)PerSec\w*><>Count'
    name: kafka_$1_$2_$3_total
    type: COUNTER
  # Jauges génériques
  - pattern: 'kafka.(\w+)<type=(.+), name=(.+), (.+)=(.+), (.+)=(.+)><>Value'
    name: kafka_$1_$2_$3
    type: GAUGE
    labels: { "$4": "$5", "$6": "$7" }
  - pattern: 'kafka.(\w+)<type=(.+), name=(.+), (.+)=(.+)><>Value'
    name: kafka_$1_$2_$3
    type: GAUGE
    labels: { "$4": "$5" }
  - pattern: 'kafka.(\w+)<type=(.+), name=(.+)><>Value'
    name: kafka_$1_$2_$3
    type: GAUGE
  # Histogrammes (latences des requêtes)
  - pattern: 'kafka.(\w+)<type=(.+), name=(.+), (.+)=(.+), (.+)=(.+)><>Count'
    name: kafka_$1_$2_$3_count
    type: COUNTER
    labels: { "$4": "$5", "$6": "$7" }
  - pattern: 'kafka.(\w+)<type=(.+), name=(.+), (.+)=(.*), (.+)=(.+)><>(\d+)thPercentile'
    name: kafka_$1_$2_$3
    type: GAUGE
    labels: { "$4": "$5", "$6": "$7", quantile: "0.$8" }
  - pattern: 'kafka.(\w+)<type=(.+), name=(.+), (.+)=(.+)><>Count'
    name: kafka_$1_$2_$3_count
    type: COUNTER
    labels: { "$4": "$5" }
  - pattern: 'kafka.(\w+)<type=(.+), name=(.+), (.+)=(.*)><>(\d+)thPercentile'
    name: kafka_$1_$2_$3
    type: GAUGE
    labels: { "$4": "$5", quantile: "0.$6" }
  - pattern: 'kafka.(\w+)<type=(.+), name=(.+)><>Count'
    name: kafka_$1_$2_$3_count
    type: COUNTER
  - pattern: 'kafka.(\w+)<type=(.+), name=(.+)><>(\d+)thPercentile'
    name: kafka_$1_$2_$3
    type: GAUGE
    labels: { quantile: "0.$4" }
EOF
chmod 644 /etc/jmx_exporter/kafka-broker.yml

On ajoute l’agent au service par un fichier complémentaire (drop-in), sans modifier l’unit d’origine :

mkdir -p /etc/systemd/system/kafka.service.d && cat > /etc/systemd/system/kafka.service.d/jmx-exporter.conf <<'EOF'
[Service]
Environment="KAFKA_OPTS=-javaagent:/opt/jmx_exporter/jmx_prometheus_javaagent-1.6.0.jar=7071:/etc/jmx_exporter/kafka-broker.yml"
EOF
systemctl daemon-reload

Redémarrage un broker à la fois, dans l’ordre dbk70, puis dbk71, puis dbk72 :

systemctl restart kafka && sleep 30 && curl -s localhost:7071/metrics | grep -E '^kafka_server_replicamanager_underreplicatedpartitions|^kafka_server_raft_current_state'

Avant de passer au broker suivant, vérifiez depuis la toolbox que toutes les partitions sont de nouveau répliquées. La commande ne doit rien afficher :

$K/kafka-topics.sh $ADM --describe --under-replicated-partitions
c) Règles pour Connect et Debezium (sur dbz70-71)
cat > /etc/jmx_exporter/kafka-connect.yml <<'EOF'
lowercaseOutputName: true
lowercaseOutputLabelNames: true
rules:
  # --- Debezium (PostgreSQL / Oracle) ---
  - pattern: 'debezium.([^:]+)<type=connector-metrics, context=([^,]+), server=([^,]+), key=([^>]+)><>RowsScanned'
    name: debezium_metrics_rowsscanned
    labels: { plugin: "$1", context: "$2", name: "$3", table: "$4" }
  - pattern: 'debezium.([^:]+)<type=connector-metrics, server=([^,]+), task=([^,]+), context=([^>]+)><>([^:]+)'
    name: debezium_metrics_$5
    labels: { plugin: "$1", name: "$2", task: "$3", context: "$4" }
  - pattern: 'debezium.([^:]+)<type=connector-metrics, context=([^,]+), server=([^>,]+)><>([^:]+)'
    name: debezium_metrics_$4
    labels: { plugin: "$1", context: "$2", name: "$3" }
  # --- Kafka Connect : statut des connecteurs et tâches (valeur texte -> 1) ---
  - pattern: 'kafka.connect<type=connector-metrics, connector=(.+)><>status: ([a-z-]+)'
    name: kafka_connect_connector_status
    value: 1
    labels: { connector: "$1", status: "$2" }
  - pattern: 'kafka.connect<type=connector-task-metrics, connector=(.+), task=(.+)><>status: ([a-z-]+)'
    name: kafka_connect_task_status
    value: 1
    labels: { connector: "$1", task: "$2", status: "$3" }
  # --- Métriques des tâches ---
  - pattern: 'kafka.connect<type=(.+)-metrics, connector=(.+), task=(.+)><>([a-z-]+)'
    name: kafka_connect_$1_$4
    labels: { connector: "$2", task: "$3" }
  # --- Worker ---
  - pattern: 'kafka.connect<type=connect-worker-metrics, connector=(.+)><>([a-z-]+)'
    name: kafka_connect_worker_$2
    labels: { connector: "$1" }
  - pattern: 'kafka.connect<type=connect-worker-metrics><>([a-z-]+)'
    name: kafka_connect_worker_$1
  - pattern: 'kafka.connect<type=connect-worker-rebalance-metrics><>([a-z-]+)'
    name: kafka_connect_worker_rebalance_$1
  - pattern: 'kafka.connect<type=connect-coordinator-metrics, client-id=(.+)><>(assigned-connectors|assigned-tasks)'
    name: kafka_connect_coordinator_$2
    labels: { client_id: "$1" }
EOF
chmod 644 /etc/jmx_exporter/kafka-connect.yml

Le drop-in redéfinit KAFKA_OPTS. Il doit donc reprendre l’option JAAS de l’API REST définie à l’étape 4 :

mkdir -p /etc/systemd/system/kafka-connect.service.d && cat > /etc/systemd/system/kafka-connect.service.d/jmx-exporter.conf <<'EOF'
[Service]
Environment="KAFKA_OPTS=-Djava.security.auth.login.config=/etc/kafka/connect-rest-jaas.conf -javaagent:/opt/jmx_exporter/jmx_prometheus_javaagent-1.6.0.jar=7072:/etc/jmx_exporter/kafka-connect.yml"
EOF
systemctl daemon-reload && systemctl restart kafka-connect && sleep 45 && curl -s localhost:7072/metrics | grep -c '^kafka_connect_worker'

➡️ Résultat attendu : un nombre supérieur à 0. Faites un worker après l’autre. Les métriques debezium_* n’apparaîtront qu’à l’étape 6, quand des connecteurs tourneront.

